   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Agency for International Development</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Tibetan Administration (CTA) Capacity Building and Sustainability Initiative (CTA-CBSI)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(India):  . ..Using FY 2022 funds, USAID/India plans to continue its support to the CTA Capacity Building and Sustainable Initiative that would take an innovative approach to build the capacity of the Central Tibetan Administration (CTA) and, strengthen CTA leadership and planning, and improve the management systems of the CTA and other Tibetan settlement institutions in India and Nepal. The main objectives of the activity is to support greater commitment from the CTA as a means to facilitate its journey to self-reliance by enhancing accountability, strengthening legislative function and processes, creating citizen-responsive governance, and preparing CTA&apos;s institutions for eventual political transition. The activity will also strengthen citizen-responsive local governance by improving the various management systems of the CTA and Tibetan settlements, which will attract the Tibetan refugees to remain in settlements, as opposed to leaving them..This implementing mechanism contributes $2.8 million in FY 2022 ESF funding to the Tibet Governance earmark of $3 million..</narrative>
  </description>
